# Overview

SLSP is an unsupervised feature selection algorithm that simultaneously:

* Preserves global similarity
* Preserves local similarity
* Learns discriminative cluster structures
* Selects informative features through sparse learning

Unlike many earlier methods that focus only on local similarity or clustering, SLSP integrates all these components into a unified optimization framework.

---

# Main Contributions

✔ Joint learning of clustering and feature selection

✔ Global similarity preservation via symmetric NMF

✔ Local similarity preservation via graph Laplacian

✔ Sparse feature selection using ℓ₂,₁ regularization

✔ Convergence-guaranteed optimization

✔ Strong performance on biological, image, voice, and artificial datasets

---

# Method

SLSP jointly optimizes:

* Global Similarity Matrix
* Cluster Assignment Matrix
* Sparse Transformation Matrix

The objective function integrates:

1. Symmetric Nonnegative Matrix Factorization
2. Spectral Analysis
3. Sparse Regression
4. Similarity Preservation

Features are ranked according to:

||wi||₂

where rows with larger norms correspond to more informative features.

---

# Why SLSP?

Many existing methods use only one or two of the following:

| Method | Local Similarity | Global Similarity | Clustering | Joint Learning |
| ------ | ---------------- | ----------------- | ---------- | -------------- |
| MCFS   | ✓                | ✗                 | ✗          | ✗              |
| UDFS   | ✓                | ✗                 | ✗          | ✓              |
| NDFS   | ✓                | ✗                 | ✓          | ✓              |
| SPFS   | ✗                | ✓                 | ✗          | ✓              |
| GLSPFS | ✓                | ✓                 | ✗          | ✓              |
| SLSP   | ✓                | ✓                 | ✓          | ✓              |

SLSP is designed to combine all four characteristics in a single framework.

